   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## <span style=\"color:red; font-size:25px\"> III. Interrupting `for` loops </span>\n",
    "\n",
    "<font size = \"4\">\n",
    "\n",
    "- Sometimes we want to halt a \"for\" loop once a condition has been met. We can do so with the `break` keyword.\n",
    "\n",
    "- Sometimes we want to skip over one pass through a \"for\" loop if some condition holds. We can do so with a `continue` keyword.\n",
    "\n",
    "Suppose we have a collection of data stored in a list and we want to compute the sum of the elements. If there is no missing or corrupted data, its straightforward to do this with a for loop:"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "b0631382",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "31.2\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "data_list = [1, 2, 13, 4, -2, 11, 2.2]\n",
    "\n",
    "data_sum = 0\n",
    "\n",
    "for value in data_list:\n",
    "    data_sum = data_sum + value \n",
    "\n",
    "print(data_sum)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9ffa082d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<font size = \"4\">\n",
    "\n",
